# Only .local/ is linked into ~. Everything below stays in the repo:
# docs and tests are for reading/running here, and system/ holds root-owned
# files that install.sh --system copies into / (a symlink from /etc into a
# user-writable repo would let anything running as you inject root code).
# Listing any pattern here replaces stow's built-in ignore list, so README is
# repeated from it.
^/README\.md
^/docs
^/tests
^/system
^/\.stow-local-ignore
